  "id": "path-coefficient",
  "term": "path coefficient",
  "definition": "A path coefficient is a numerical value in a structural equation model that shows the direction and strength of the relationship from one variable to another. In this packet, standardized path coefficients are used to indicate how strongly one factor predicts another, either directly or as part of a mediated pathway.",
